Join SFT copied-source custody to frame admission

Reserve the complete frame queue, copied-source slot and stream credit as one
local admission. Reuse the r10 source channel at explicit r13 with two slots;
embed its offer in FrameCommit instead of sending a separate control Offer.
Keep pixels owned across Prepared/terminal and release only on exact source
evidence or a proved pre-admission refusal. Contradictory refusals and unknown
custody fail closed. Existing negotiation defaults remain unchanged.

Paired independent SDK checks: 968 Rust workspace tests, full C make check,
strict clippy/rustdoc, C ASan/UBSan, four mutation failures and regressions for
Prepared-before-refusal. Evidence: sophia-frame-client-source-join-01, seal
4e5583b9f9a3018bca46d257f569f245cf98cf642166db2701be38daad8833f1.

No host pin import, real producer adoption, native or performance claim.
